<p>The <strong>Fryline under desk elliptical</strong>, listed as the FRYLINE Ellipse Leg Exerciser, is a budget manual elliptical machine you use from your chair. You set it on the floor, rest your feet on the pedals and move them in a smooth oval while you work, read or watch TV. It is built for light, all-day movement rather than heavy workouts.</p>
<p>Our verdict: the Fryline elliptical machine is a reasonable low-cost way to start moving more at your desk, especially for seniors and light users. Its lighter build and basic display are the trade-offs for the price. If you want something sturdier or quieter, we compare it with three proven alternatives below.</p>
