<h2>What Is the Fryline Under Desk Elliptical?</h2>
<p>The Fryline is a compact seated elliptical, sometimes called a leg exerciser. It has two foot platforms on short crank arms, a flywheel inside a housing, adjustable resistance and a small display. There is no motor, so every stride comes from your legs.</p>
<p>That simple design is the point. There is no app to pair, no cord to route and almost nothing to learn. You sit down, start pedaling and adjust the resistance until it feels comfortable. The display shows basic figures such as time and estimated calories, which are useful for tracking consistency rather than precise effort.</p>
<h3>The name: Fryline vs FRYLINE Ellipse Leg Exerciser</h3>
<p>If you searched for "Fryline" on its own, you were most likely looking for this machine. The brand sells it under the longer FRYLINE Ellipse Leg Exerciser name, and owner reviews use both. They refer to the same type of compact seated elliptical.</p>

